WEBVTT

00:13.972 --> 00:15.932
Oh, my, Master! Hello there!

00:16.016 --> 00:17.851
Hello! Another hot day, eh?

00:17.934 --> 00:20.979
It sure is!
Maybe there'll be an evening squall.

00:21.062 --> 00:23.815
Right. I'll just walk in it to rinse off!

00:25.483 --> 00:27.360
Hey Master, how about a trim?

00:27.444 --> 00:30.655
Well, let's see. It's pretty long now.

00:30.739 --> 00:32.907
Wait, I just got it cut
the day before yesterday!

00:33.825 --> 00:34.993
You're right, you did!

00:38.246 --> 00:40.415
The festival's coming up soon.

00:40.498 --> 00:43.918
Yeah. It'll be another
lively one this year, I bet.

00:46.796 --> 00:49.174
There you go.
It's hot today, so here's an extra scoop.

00:49.257 --> 00:51.301
Are you sure? Thanks for the trouble.

00:51.384 --> 00:55.138
Oh, listen, you know that young girl
apprentice who you often bring here?

00:55.221 --> 00:58.058
She came the other day with some friends.

00:58.808 --> 01:01.019
She's such a cheerful,
sweet girl, isn't she?

01:01.102 --> 01:01.978
That Akane!

01:02.062 --> 01:06.149
Oh? I wonder who her master could be?

01:06.232 --> 01:10.487
Right! I hear that this master of hers
is a big fan of ice cream!

01:10.570 --> 01:13.573
Whoops, if I stand here chatting,
my ice cream will melt!

01:13.656 --> 01:16.201
- See you around!
- Thank you very much!

01:27.003 --> 01:28.546
I'm coming in!

01:29.422 --> 01:30.924
Oh, Master!

01:31.007 --> 01:35.094
I know how busy you are,
so thanks for stopping by!

01:35.178 --> 01:37.680
It's nothing. I was taking a walk, anyway.

01:37.764 --> 01:40.475
So how's the festival prep going?
Everything okay?

01:40.558 --> 01:42.852
Yes, it's more or less locked down.

01:42.936 --> 01:46.314
Year after year, you and your apprentices
give it a shot in the arm,

01:46.397 --> 01:48.066
so we can expect a big crowd.

01:48.149 --> 01:49.275
We really appreciate it!

01:49.359 --> 01:52.946
Hey, come on.
We're looking forward to it, too.

01:53.029 --> 01:56.699
Do you think your apprentices
will be able to join us again?

01:56.783 --> 01:58.618
Yes. Same as last year.

01:58.701 --> 02:00.870
Maikeru, Koguma, Kyoji, Guriko.

02:00.954 --> 02:02.372
The Mismatched Four!

02:02.455 --> 02:03.832
I'm leaving them in your hands!

02:04.624 --> 02:06.376
Wow, we'd appreciate that!

02:06.459 --> 02:10.880
And next year, I think
we'll be getting one more little rebel.

02:10.964 --> 02:13.591
- Oh?
- Really? A new apprentice, then?

02:13.675 --> 02:14.592
What's their name?

02:15.635 --> 02:18.555
We haven't decided on a stage name yet.

02:18.638 --> 02:21.683
Since the apprenticeship
is a little ways off.

02:21.766 --> 02:23.518
Well, that's something to look forward to!

02:24.102 --> 02:27.689
You choose your apprentice's
stage name, right?

02:27.772 --> 02:29.732
How do you come up with them?

02:30.233 --> 02:32.777
Whatever hits me on a whim.

02:34.571 --> 02:38.199
If there's anything I can help with,
let me know anytime.

02:38.283 --> 02:40.702
- Okay, see you.
- Take care!

02:52.213 --> 02:54.007
Her name, huh?

04:26.516 --> 04:28.226
TWELFTH STORY
GRADUATION

04:29.102 --> 04:32.814
Oh, so you won that Rakugo tournament?

04:32.897 --> 04:33.898
Wow, lukewarm reaction!

04:34.649 --> 04:35.900
Is that all you've got?

04:35.984 --> 04:38.403
What? You won? Congrats!

04:39.237 --> 04:41.572
- Something like that.
- Nope, sorry.

04:41.656 --> 04:45.368
I mean, I always thought
you were gonna win.

04:45.451 --> 04:46.286
Anyway...

04:46.369 --> 04:48.663
This is for Dad!

04:49.414 --> 04:54.377
I was more worried that you might
snap and cause a huge uproar.

04:54.460 --> 04:56.379
Just who do you think I am?

04:57.297 --> 04:59.090
Well, for what he did to you guys,

04:59.173 --> 05:01.509
an outburst like that
would've been warranted.

05:02.468 --> 05:04.178
Still, what good would that do?

05:05.221 --> 05:07.473
If I can't convince him with my art,
there's no point.

05:09.642 --> 05:11.060
Yeah?

05:12.145 --> 05:13.354
Why are you snickering like that?

05:13.438 --> 05:15.481
No reason!

05:15.565 --> 05:18.067
It just hit me that
you've made the transition

05:18.151 --> 05:20.945
from a Rakugoka's daughter
to a Rakugoka yourself.

05:22.155 --> 05:23.406
Oh, yeah?

05:23.489 --> 05:25.408
Cool thing to say for you, Jumbo.

05:25.491 --> 05:27.410
What do you mean, "for you"?

05:28.536 --> 05:29.787
All right, I'm out of here.

05:29.871 --> 05:33.082
You better go tell the principal
in person that you won.

05:33.166 --> 05:35.043
- Right! Take care!
- Sure.

05:36.294 --> 05:37.545
Akane!

05:39.839 --> 05:40.673
Lisa?

05:40.757 --> 05:42.508
Yuka, too? What's going on?

05:42.592 --> 05:44.010
Take a look at this! This!

05:46.429 --> 05:47.555
What is this?

05:47.638 --> 05:51.768
The teen girl Rakugo prodigy
who blew Issho Arakawa away.

05:52.351 --> 05:55.146
With artistry of such unfathomable
maturity, given her youth,

05:55.730 --> 05:58.775
she captivated not only the audience,
but also the panel of judges,

05:58.858 --> 06:03.029
led by the very best of this era,
Issho Arakawa.

06:05.031 --> 06:09.577
Well, well, people sure have
a thing for the youngsters!

06:10.578 --> 06:15.083
Look at them, so exhilarated
over an amateur girl.

06:15.166 --> 06:16.709
RYU'UN KENPUTEI

06:16.793 --> 06:19.587
Oh, I beg your pardon.

06:19.670 --> 06:21.631
Please don't take that the wrong way.

06:21.714 --> 06:23.591
Master Shiguma.

06:23.674 --> 06:25.843
There's no reason why I would be offended.

06:25.927 --> 06:27.637
Is that right?

06:27.720 --> 06:29.138
But this girl...

06:29.222 --> 06:31.349
She's your apprentice, isn't she?

06:31.933 --> 06:34.310
Her narrative style is exactly like yours.

06:34.393 --> 06:36.020
Or maybe I should say...

06:37.021 --> 06:39.482
So "Arakawa" strikes again?

06:41.692 --> 06:42.985
SHOMEI TSUBAKIYA

06:43.069 --> 06:45.196
I have nothing against him thriving,

06:45.279 --> 06:47.198
but Master Issho has an arrogant attitude,

06:47.281 --> 06:50.451
like he's the one carrying
the Rakugo industry on his shoulders.

06:50.535 --> 06:53.037
Not to mention his school's
arbitrary standards for promotion

06:53.121 --> 06:55.915
such as elevating someone to Futatsume
only two years into his apprenticeship.

06:55.998 --> 06:58.167
He can't just do as he sees fit, or we--

06:58.251 --> 07:01.254
I agree, Master Issho can be a bit much.

07:01.921 --> 07:04.924
But wouldn't you say
that Kaisei's promotion turned out okay?

07:05.007 --> 07:05.716
CHOCHO KONJAKUTEI

07:05.800 --> 07:08.886
He's young, but he's capable,
and has drawing power, after all.

07:08.970 --> 07:09.804
But...

07:09.887 --> 07:13.766
his promotion was,
by most standards, too premature.

07:13.850 --> 07:15.768
A lot of people
are still grumbling about it.

07:16.561 --> 07:18.104
Well, what do you expect?

07:18.187 --> 07:20.690
Nothing irritates people more than
the sight of someone else

07:20.773 --> 07:22.275
getting preferential treatment.

07:22.358 --> 07:23.192
URARA RANSAIKA

07:23.276 --> 07:27.905
If it irritates you, then all
you have to do is act just like Arakawa.

07:30.116 --> 07:34.412
You can only be arrogant if you're
talented enough to get away with it.

07:35.496 --> 07:38.166
Surely, people don't follow
the rules because

07:38.249 --> 07:39.959
they're unable to assert themselves.

07:40.042 --> 07:40.877
ENSO SANMEITEI

07:40.960 --> 07:42.795
With all due respect, sir...

07:42.879 --> 07:45.006
All right, that's enough.

07:45.089 --> 07:47.467
Shomei, take a seat now.

07:50.344 --> 07:53.222
The reason we,
the Rakugo Federation, exists

07:53.806 --> 07:56.434
is to revitalize the Rakugo industry.

07:56.517 --> 07:58.936
So let's enjoy ourselves doing that.

07:59.020 --> 07:59.854
MIROKU KASHIWAYA

07:59.937 --> 08:03.316
That being said,
I do understand how you all feel.

08:03.983 --> 08:06.277
Maybe your people
are getting a bit too carried away.

08:07.111 --> 08:08.613
Don't you think so, Arakawa?

08:12.575 --> 08:15.411
Now, now, wake up!

08:15.495 --> 08:16.787
Jugemu Jugemu Goko-no-surikirezu

08:16.871 --> 08:18.456
Kaijari-suigyo no Suigyo-matsu
Ungyo-matsu Furai-matsu

08:18.539 --> 08:20.374
Kuu-neru tokoro ni Sumu tokoro
Yaburakoji no Burakoji

08:20.458 --> 08:22.084
Paipo-Paipo-Paipo no
Shuringan Shuringan no--

08:22.168 --> 08:23.085
Ma'am!

08:23.169 --> 08:25.505
I'm going to be late for school,
so I'll go on ahead!

08:25.588 --> 08:28.090
Well, well! This is magnificent! Truly!

08:28.174 --> 08:32.220
A student of ours making her mark
in the traditional arts.

08:32.303 --> 08:35.056
And winning, no less!
You sure did a great job.

08:35.139 --> 08:37.850
Really, you're at the top of the top.
The pinnacle!

08:37.934 --> 08:39.519
Keep pushing onward
to the Eiger North Face!

08:39.602 --> 08:41.354
Onward, onward!

08:41.437 --> 08:44.857
- Oh, thank you very much!
- Onward!

08:44.941 --> 08:49.070
Oh, pardon me!
Mountain climbing is my hobby, see.

08:49.153 --> 08:51.239
All right, let's get one
made for you right away.

08:51.322 --> 08:53.616
We need to celebrate, after all!
You know? That!

08:54.659 --> 08:55.618
That?

08:56.536 --> 08:57.453
CONGRATULATIONS STUDENT RAKUGO COMPETITION
KARAKU CUP WINNER! MS. AKANE OSAKI

08:57.537 --> 09:00.414
By that, you mean this?

09:01.415 --> 09:03.834
Oh, wow! Your name is huge!

09:03.918 --> 09:05.086
It's Insta-worthy.

09:05.169 --> 09:06.754
Come on! Strike a pose, Akane!

09:06.837 --> 09:08.798
Great smile!

09:08.881 --> 09:10.758
YEAR 3, CLASS 2

09:10.841 --> 09:12.802
Hey, Osaki, how long
have you been doing Rakugo?

09:12.885 --> 09:14.720
Um, well, for a pretty long time.

09:14.804 --> 09:17.431
- Do you have, like, a partner?
- No, it's not stand-up.

09:17.515 --> 09:19.183
Will you compete
in the comedy tournaments?

09:19.267 --> 09:20.101
Nope, not doing that.

09:20.184 --> 09:22.645
If you're on TV,
get me an idol singer's autograph!

09:22.728 --> 09:24.564
Uh, no, that's not happening, okay?

09:24.647 --> 09:27.316
Hey, come on, just let me get a photo!
Please?

09:27.400 --> 09:29.068
- Sorry! I'm serious, I can't do that!
- Aww.

09:29.151 --> 09:30.861
Hey, there she is!

09:30.945 --> 09:32.655
- What do you mean?
- Osaki-senpai,

09:32.738 --> 09:36.033
- can we get a selfie with you?
- Nope! Not happening! No way!

09:37.493 --> 09:39.453
Hey, I wonder where she ran off to?

09:39.537 --> 09:40.663
Over there, maybe?

09:40.746 --> 09:41.747
- That way?
- Yeah.

09:42.790 --> 09:43.958
Hey, she's not here.

09:44.041 --> 09:45.418
Ms. Osaki?

09:47.753 --> 09:48.588
LANGUAGE ARTS CENTER

09:48.671 --> 09:50.381
Well, that sounds like a hassle.

09:50.464 --> 09:53.175
But isn't Rakugo all about popularity?

09:53.259 --> 09:56.637
I don't think it's a bad thing
to draw a lot of attention.

09:56.721 --> 09:59.265
Well, sure, I totally appreciate it.

09:59.348 --> 10:00.975
But it's happening so fast.

10:01.559 --> 10:05.688
Your victory in the Karaku Cup is
something that you worked hard to achieve.

10:05.771 --> 10:08.107
I think you can hold your head up high.

10:10.026 --> 10:13.029
What, so you were running away
during lunch recess?

10:13.112 --> 10:14.155
That's hilarious!

10:14.238 --> 10:16.032
It's not funny.

10:16.616 --> 10:18.909
I might have to skip school for a while.

10:20.161 --> 10:23.539
- Still, how crazy is this?
- What?

10:23.623 --> 10:25.916
I knew you were planning
to become a Rakugoka,

10:26.000 --> 10:29.587
but now I know how hard
you've been training and all.

10:29.670 --> 10:32.298
- Isn't that amazing?
- Amazing.

10:34.133 --> 10:36.010
My training hasn't even begun yet.

10:36.093 --> 10:38.012
Actually, it'll probably continue
for the rest of my life.

10:38.721 --> 10:41.140
There are tons of people
who've been at it for over 50 years.

10:41.223 --> 10:43.142
Whoa, 50 years? Unbelievable.

10:43.225 --> 10:45.811
So you see,
I've got such a long way to go.

10:45.895 --> 10:48.189
Hey, don't talk like that!

10:48.272 --> 10:51.025
I mean, I'm using this
to convince my parents, you know.

10:51.108 --> 10:51.942
Convince them?

10:52.026 --> 10:53.861
Right. I've made up my mind.

10:53.944 --> 10:56.238
Instead of junior college,
I'm gonna try to get in a trade school.

10:56.322 --> 10:58.532
I'm seriously going to pursue a career
as a hair and makeup artist!

10:58.616 --> 10:59.867
Huh? For real?

10:59.950 --> 11:01.952
I'm not about to lose to you, Akane!

11:02.036 --> 11:03.079
Right, Yuka?

11:03.162 --> 11:06.165
Huh? Yuka, you're taking the entrance exam
for Shuei University, right?

11:06.248 --> 11:10.002
Yes. But while I study for that exam,
I'm going to keep on studying art.

11:11.003 --> 11:14.715
Goal. To make my debut
as an illustrator when I get into college.

11:15.883 --> 11:18.677
- Wow, both of you are on fire!
- Well, yeah.

11:19.261 --> 11:21.889
How can we not get motivated
after seeing this?

11:22.515 --> 11:26.102
I'll bet there are others.
People who got some courage from you.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.064
Is that right?

11:31.774 --> 11:33.526
I know it's obvious,

11:33.609 --> 11:37.238
but once we graduate, we're all
going off on our respective paths.

11:37.947 --> 11:38.989
Yeah.

11:39.490 --> 11:43.077
Hey, so we've only got six months left
to be high school girls!

11:43.160 --> 11:44.203
That went by so fast.

11:45.079 --> 11:46.705
Nope, we're not done yet!

11:46.789 --> 11:50.167
We're going to enjoy
the last six months to the max!

11:50.751 --> 11:52.628
Yeah!

11:53.295 --> 11:57.091
You said that you wanted to take part
in practice at the university, right?

11:57.174 --> 12:00.344
Didn't you just finish competing
in the interscholastic meet?

12:00.428 --> 12:01.804
Yes, that's right.

12:02.638 --> 12:05.558
But I only made it to the quarterfinals.

12:06.976 --> 12:08.769
So I thought, "I don't want to lose."

12:08.853 --> 12:10.729
That's a great attitude to have!

12:11.355 --> 12:13.023
I'll set it up for you.

12:13.107 --> 12:15.818
Make sure you don't let your studies
fall by the wayside, all right?

12:15.901 --> 12:17.903
Yes, sir! Thank you for your support, sir!

12:17.987 --> 12:18.821
Right.

12:20.072 --> 12:21.282
I'm so sorry.

12:21.365 --> 12:24.743
Oh, no, I really don't mind at all.

12:24.827 --> 12:26.245
I'm so ashamed.

12:26.328 --> 12:29.748
To commit such a blunder
when I'm your elder fellow apprentice!

12:29.832 --> 12:31.417
Seriously, it's all good.

12:31.500 --> 12:34.670
And thanks to that,
I realized what I was lacking.

12:35.254 --> 12:36.130
Ani-san.

12:36.213 --> 12:38.674
Please show me how to play the taiko,
and how to dance!

12:40.092 --> 12:41.427
Wait, why are you looking at me like that?

12:41.510 --> 12:44.680
Well, both Koguma Ani-san
and Guriko said to me...

12:44.763 --> 12:48.142
"Akane will be after you
to teach her taiko and dance, for sure!"

12:48.225 --> 12:51.187
They were so spot-on
that I couldn't help it.

12:51.270 --> 12:52.438
Cringe!

12:53.439 --> 12:55.274
That's the spirit!

12:55.357 --> 12:56.525
But don't get greedy.

12:57.109 --> 12:59.403
We'll start with taiko.

13:00.321 --> 13:01.697
What I'm about to play

13:01.780 --> 13:05.117
is the Ichiban-daiko that you hear
when the entertainment hall opens.

13:28.140 --> 13:29.433
Hey, it's Dad!

13:39.235 --> 13:42.029
I don't know. I'm just worried, I guess?

13:43.447 --> 13:44.782
Worried?

13:44.865 --> 13:46.283
What do you mean by that?

13:46.367 --> 13:47.201
COIN LAUNDRY TSUZUKI

13:47.284 --> 13:49.370
Well, see, you know what I mean.

13:49.453 --> 13:50.829
They're just not open about it,

13:50.913 --> 13:53.249
but because of how Master Issho
behaves and acts,

13:53.332 --> 13:56.752
there are more than a few Rakugoka
who don't take kindly to "Arakawa."

13:57.753 --> 14:00.005
And now, with that going on,
this article comes out.

14:01.048 --> 14:05.511
Master Issho might be using
this competition

14:05.594 --> 14:08.013
to produce the next Kaisei Arakawa.

14:08.597 --> 14:10.849
That's a hot topic
even at our school, you know.

14:14.270 --> 14:15.813
The hands that strike this taiko

14:16.480 --> 14:20.234
are calling out to the audience
to keep coming, more and more.

14:27.908 --> 14:29.410
Give it a try.

14:29.493 --> 14:30.619
Right!

14:33.372 --> 14:36.333
That article about the Karaku Cup...
It's getting a lot of buzz, huh?

14:36.417 --> 14:38.919
Ani-san, you can see
online articles, then?

14:39.003 --> 14:40.754
Don't ever underestimate a flip phone!

14:41.422 --> 14:46.886
Well, they hung a banner at school, and
all these people come up to talk to me.

14:46.969 --> 14:48.971
It makes me feel like
a celebrity or something.

14:49.847 --> 14:51.682
And I'm not sure how I feel about that.

14:53.100 --> 14:56.145
I'm glad that it makes them happy,
but still...

14:59.732 --> 15:01.775
You can't say that I blew him away.

15:03.652 --> 15:07.197
This is just me guessing...

15:07.281 --> 15:09.742
But all those negative feelings
towards Master Issho...

15:09.825 --> 15:12.328
might be turned to Akane now.

15:13.787 --> 15:17.166
If it seemed like it had gone to her head,
I knew I'd have to set her straight.

15:17.249 --> 15:18.542
but my fears were unfounded.

15:19.627 --> 15:21.545
She'll start her official training
six months from now.

15:22.254 --> 15:24.423
The Zenza training
might be grueling for her.

15:25.257 --> 15:28.135
But if anyone,
my younger fellow apprentice can...

15:34.058 --> 15:39.855
123RD RYOKUGYOKU HIGH SCHOOL
GRADUATION

15:41.273 --> 15:43.567
- Shota Ehara.
- Yes, ma'am!

15:46.820 --> 15:49.198
- Akane Osaki.
- Yes, ma'am!

15:56.330 --> 15:57.581
Congratulations.

16:00.125 --> 16:01.710
GRADUATION CERTIFICATE

16:12.221 --> 16:14.682
Hey, Master! Where are you going?

16:14.765 --> 16:16.016
I'm going for a walk.

16:28.404 --> 16:31.865
Compared to soba,
udon seems a little heavier.

16:31.949 --> 16:33.492
Express the weight of it.

16:55.389 --> 16:56.932
Well? Is that tasty?

16:57.016 --> 16:58.058
Yes.

16:58.142 --> 17:00.060
The syrup's dripping.

17:00.144 --> 17:01.103
I'm fine.

17:01.186 --> 17:03.939
Here, give it to me.
I'll fix it so it doesn't drip.

17:04.023 --> 17:04.982
Nope.

17:23.876 --> 17:25.753
- Come on, get in the picture.
- But...

17:25.836 --> 17:27.004
This way, this way!

17:42.519 --> 17:43.896
Akane.

17:48.901 --> 17:49.943
I'm home.

18:19.932 --> 18:22.309
Jugemu Jugemu...

18:23.811 --> 18:27.106
Goko-no-surikirezu...

18:55.175 --> 18:56.301
Hello!

18:56.385 --> 18:59.263
Hello! It's the liquor store!

18:59.930 --> 19:01.181
Hello?

19:01.682 --> 19:04.101
Hello! It's the liquor store!

19:04.184 --> 19:06.562
I have a delivery for you.

19:06.645 --> 19:08.397
Hello?

19:08.480 --> 19:09.523
Hey there!

19:09.606 --> 19:12.693
Whoa! M-Master, you're answering the door?

19:12.776 --> 19:16.113
Well, the thing is,
nobody's around this morning.

19:16.196 --> 19:17.906
Oh, is that right?

19:17.990 --> 19:19.867
So, what've you got?

19:19.950 --> 19:21.076
Oh, this is it.

19:21.160 --> 19:23.370
- Here you go.
- Right.

19:23.453 --> 19:24.872
Thanks for your business!

19:24.955 --> 19:26.165
Good work!

19:26.248 --> 19:27.457
Oh, good work!

19:27.541 --> 19:30.210
Hey! Akane! Thanks!

19:30.794 --> 19:32.379
Good morning!

19:32.462 --> 19:33.547
Morning.

19:33.630 --> 19:34.715
Wanna crack one open?

19:34.798 --> 19:36.675
You little fool.

19:36.758 --> 19:37.801
Bring me some tea.

19:37.885 --> 19:39.011
Right!

19:42.848 --> 19:45.559
First, congratulations on graduating.

19:45.642 --> 19:47.144
Thank you very much.

19:47.227 --> 19:48.395
Just as I promised,

19:48.478 --> 19:51.982
I'm granting you permission
to officially become my apprentice.

19:52.816 --> 19:54.193
Thank you very much.

19:54.276 --> 19:58.113
Going from trainee to Zenza means you'll
be working at the entertainment halls.

19:58.197 --> 20:00.240
- Right.
- Give it all you've got.

20:00.324 --> 20:01.575
I'll do my best!

20:02.451 --> 20:03.660
And one more thing.

20:03.744 --> 20:05.287
About your stage name...

20:05.370 --> 20:06.997
- Master!
- Hm?

20:07.080 --> 20:10.250
I can't tell you how grateful I am
to receive my name from you!

20:10.334 --> 20:14.046
But my goal is to make Issho Arakawa
acknowledge Dad's Rakugo,

20:14.129 --> 20:16.256
and to become a Shin'uchi.

20:16.340 --> 20:20.636
I believe I can only become a full-fledged
Rakugoka when I've avenged my dad.

20:21.136 --> 20:23.096
And so, once I've become a Shin'uchi,

20:23.180 --> 20:26.934
that's when I'd like to revisit this and
receive my name from you as a Rakugoka.

20:27.434 --> 20:29.728
Please, if you could please humor me.

20:32.397 --> 20:35.484
I know that as your apprentice,
I'm out of line, talking this way!

20:35.567 --> 20:38.070
But until I become a Shin'uchi...

20:38.153 --> 20:39.571
Please, let me keep the name Akane.

20:41.448 --> 20:43.325
ARAKAWA

20:47.204 --> 20:49.998
AKANE

20:50.832 --> 20:53.710
That's what I thought you'd say.

20:53.794 --> 20:55.254
Master.

20:57.256 --> 21:01.468
The day you become a Shin'uchi,
I'll give you the best name ever.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.637
If you don't make it,
then that'll be that.

21:04.263 --> 21:05.639
Does that sound good?

21:06.807 --> 21:07.766
Yes!

21:11.979 --> 21:16.650
CONGRATULATIONS
GRADUATION & APPRENTICESHIP

21:16.733 --> 21:19.486
Celebrate, celebrate!

21:19.569 --> 21:22.281
Celebrate, celebrate!

21:22.364 --> 21:24.658
Celebrate, celebrate!

21:24.741 --> 21:27.619
Celebrate, celebrate!

21:27.703 --> 21:30.580
Celebrate graduation!

21:30.664 --> 21:33.542
Celebrate apprenticeship!

21:33.625 --> 21:36.378
Celebrate graduation!

21:36.461 --> 21:39.339
Celebrate apprenticeship!

21:39.423 --> 21:42.009
All right, Akane,
let's hear your Ichiban-daiko!

21:42.092 --> 21:43.260
You got it!

21:59.192 --> 22:00.152
All right!

22:00.235 --> 22:02.904
ZENZA TRAINING BEGINS

23:33.787 --> 23:35.539
Akane Small Talk!

23:39.251 --> 23:41.169
I'm so thrilled
to receive my theater name!

23:41.253 --> 23:45.298
Right. This one was a struggle for me,
but I'm glad that it's settled now.

23:45.382 --> 23:48.135
From here on in, work hard as a Zenza.

23:48.218 --> 23:50.762
Right! Um, you said it was a struggle.

23:50.846 --> 23:52.973
Does that mean there were
other names you had in mind?

23:53.056 --> 23:54.182
Well, I guess you could say that.

23:54.266 --> 23:57.144
Really? I want to know!
What kind of names?

23:57.227 --> 23:58.854
Don't ask foolish questions.

23:58.937 --> 24:00.313
Well, there were all kinds.

24:00.397 --> 24:02.023
One of the most typical ways

24:02.107 --> 24:05.152
is to come up with a name containing
one character from the master's name.

24:05.235 --> 24:06.361
Your name?

24:06.444 --> 24:08.738
I took the "shi" from "Shiguma"
for "Shinta,"

24:08.822 --> 24:11.032
and the "guma" from "Shiguma"
for "Koguma."

24:11.116 --> 24:12.659
Oh, I see.

24:12.742 --> 24:14.661
You need to apply yourself,
so that one day,

24:14.744 --> 24:18.498
when you become a Shin'uchi,
you'll be able to live up to a fine name.

24:20.083 --> 24:22.961
Aka. Huh? Aka...

24:23.044 --> 24:25.213
Hm? What's eating you?

24:25.297 --> 24:28.133
Oh, actually, I was wondering
what kind of name I'd give,

24:28.216 --> 24:29.509
if I ever took on an apprentice.

24:29.593 --> 24:31.303
I'd take the "Aka" from "Akane" and...

24:31.386 --> 24:33.054
Um, "Aka-tombo"?

24:33.138 --> 24:34.764
"Account"?

24:35.515 --> 24:38.059
"Main Account"? "Other Account"?

24:39.436 --> 24:40.520
"Shadow Account"?

24:40.604 --> 24:43.607
You little fool!
You're going about it all wrong!

24:43.690 --> 24:45.358
That's "Akarasama"!
Meaning, "clear as day"!
